Title: Fix dropped Greek tau glyph in manuscript PDF
Created: 2026-06-10
Author: HDMX-coding-agent

--- log ---
2026-06-10T21:26Z HDMX-coding-agent created

--- body ---
## Context
`slides/manuscript/main.md` used a literal Greek τ (U+03C4) in prose for the
"Kendall τ" statistic (4 occurrences: lines ~180, 505, 507×2). Tectonic's text
font `lmroman10-regular` has no glyph for U+03C4, so on build it emitted
`Missing character: There is no τ (U+03C4)` and **silently dropped** the symbol —
the PDF read "Kendall  = +0.215". A content defect, not a typesetting nit.

Found while rebuilding `manuscript/main.pdf` after installing pandoc-crossref.
Sibling symbols on the same lines (ρ, ≤, ×) rendered fine — only τ was missing
from the text font — so the fix is scoped to τ alone.

## Actions
1. Replace each literal `τ` with math-mode `$\tau$` in `main.md` (math font has
   the glyph; renders as math-italic 𝜏).

## Verification
- [x] `make manuscript/main.pdf` emits no `U+03C4` / tau missing-character warning
- [x] `pdftotext main.pdf | grep Kendall` shows `Kendall 𝜏` (glyph present)

## Exit criteria
- No literal U+03C4 remains in `main.md`; PDF renders the τ symbol.
